    "summary": "In Alabama, resistance to data centers is strongest in Morgan County (score 0.92), where the commission passed a 12-month moratorium that it later extended and Somerville and Trinity added their own, and in Baldwin County (0.90), where a 180-day moratorium on rezonings and new data centers is in place. Jefferson County (0.88) and Shelby County (0.88) also stand out, with moratoria in Homewood, Pinson, Tarrant, Chelsea, Helena and Westover, and Bessemer's Project Marvel backlash unseated two councilmembers. Resistance is weaker in Lowndes County, where a 3-2 commission majority granted Project Red Clay tax abatements despite organized opposition and lawsuits, in Jackson and Montgomery counties, where local leaders back Google and Meta, and in Tuscaloosa County (0.40), the only county predicted to approve, as Brookwood and the abatement board advanced Applied Digital's project."
