    "summary": "Texas resistance is strongest in Hays, Denton, Cameron and Lubbock counties (each scored 0.88-0.9), where local bodies have adopted or begun moratoria or suspensions: Hays commissioners voted 5-0 to suspend discretionary approvals and San Marcos rejected the 380 MW Highlander project, Denton's council started the moratorium process, Brownsville gave final approval to a 90-day pause, and Lubbock moved toward a moratorium after a petition with 3,900+ signatures. Caldwell, Tarrant, Somervell, Brazoria, Hood and Val Verde also scored high on moratoria, incentive suspensions or denials, and Hood, Leon and Brazoria rejected specific projects or abatements. Counties like Pecos, Williamson, Young and Carson scored lowest because their officials approved projects despite organized opposition, and many counties note that Texas law limits their power to block projects in unincorporated areas."
